>>LLM is a AI model(based on neural network) Designed to understand and generate human language. ex- gemini , gpt, llama.These take input, process and generates output.
Its trained on huge amount of text.ex- the sun rises in the ____. It can predicts easily what comes next.Model assigns probablities to the tokens. LLM calculates the mathematical probability of every word in its vocabulary and picks the most likely next word.
  • Pre-training: The model reads billions of pages of text from the internet (books, articles, websites). It learns grammar, facts, and how words relate to each other by constantly guessing the hidden next word in a sentence.
  • Fine-Tuning: Human trainers guide the model to make it helpful and safe. It learns to follow instructions (like "summarize this") instead of just randomly continuing a sentence.
>>Processing :-
  -Tokenization: The LLM breaks your sentence down into smaller pieces called tokens (words or parts of words). It cannot read full words like humans do.ex- "'Hello' ',' 'how' 'are' 'you'?" .tokenization depends on the model we use.
  -Vector Conversion: It turns these tokens into long lists of numbers (called embeddings). These numbers represent the meaning and context of your words.ex- "I love india". //vector for I -->[0.01 ,0.59,0.56,0.6,0.2]  , vector for love --> [0.44,0.25,0.54,0.54,068].Different llm models (and also different tokenizer), can have different vectors.
  -Context Analysis:Transformer, the model analyzes how every word in your prompt relates to every other word to fully understand what you are asking.ex- man picks up ball , becoz it was small ,here "it" contexts to ball or man. Tells importance of tokens.
  -Prediction
>>Parameters:are the internal settings or "knobs" that the model adjusts during training to learn the relationships between words, think it as the neurons or connections in a digital brain.• Having more parameters means the model can create a much more detailed map of how all those words and concepts relate to one another.
 How Parameters Work :-
  •Weights and Biases: A parameter is essentially a mathematical number (a weight). When you give the model a prompt, the text is converted into numbers and multiplied by these billions of parameters to calculate the most logical next word.
  •The Learning Process: During training, the model starts with random parameters and makes mistakes. As it reads text, it tweaks these billions of numbers until it can accurately predict the correct words. Once training is done, these parameters are frozen.

>>Speech Recognisation & LLM :- llm converts only text to intelligent text.

>>Open-Source:- are publicly released for anyone to download, inspect, run locally, and modify ,Unlike closed-source or proprietary models (like OpenAI's GPT series or Anthropic's Claude), which are locked behind paid APIs and treated as corporate secrets, open-source models give developers full visibility and control.

